WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.006 --> 00:00:01.950
(soft music)
(audience applauds)

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.360
- [Kelly] I feel like I missed the memo

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.100
of cute, pantsuit outfit today.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.080
Like, I was like "Wait, what?
Y'all look so adorable".

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:07.913
Nice to see you.
- Nice to see you too.

00:00:07.913 --> 00:00:08.850
- [Kelly] You know each other, right?

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.683
- Yes, we're besties.

00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:10.680
- Yeah, I taught her how to ski.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.030
(audience laughs)

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.200
- I am amazing.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.020
So wait, you were skiing
in Iceland this summer

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.360
and this video is amazing
for a couple reasons,

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.893
but what's going on here?

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.220
- [Lindsey] That is a
helicopter picking me up,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.700
or dropping me off at about
one o'clock in the morning.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.590
At that time of year, the sun doesn't set.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.580
So, it was crazy.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.280
One of the most crazy
experiences of my life.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.379
Helicopter skiing at one in the morning.

00:00:34.379 --> 00:00:35.212
(Lindsey chuckles)

00:00:35.212 --> 00:00:38.013
- I love how different
people can be, you know?

00:00:38.013 --> 00:00:38.846
(audience laughs)

00:00:38.846 --> 00:00:40.560
Isn't that awesome? There's
like, room for all of us.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.727
Because I'm just like, if
one of my girls was like,

00:00:42.727 --> 00:00:43.560
"You know what I'm gonna do,

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.670
and you should do it with me,

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:48.300
is wake up at midnight
and then go skiing".

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.480
Getting dropped off by a
helicopter, which in those winds,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.150
like a helicopter can't be
like, your safest route.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.500
- [Lindsey] No, it's probably not.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.868
I mean, you know, a trail lift
would be probably, more safe.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:58.701
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:58.701 --> 00:00:59.610
- [Lindsey] But yeah, it's,

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.620
skiing is dangerous enough as it is.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.453
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:02.453 --> 00:01:03.520
- Add, you know...
- Yeah.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.250
- I would...
- Injury on that one, but...

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.540
- I would like to interrupt and say that

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.430
her heliskiing is probably safer

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.290
than with her downhill skiing.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.910
Because that's what's dangerous.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.340
You know, when she was
skiing at that, like,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.960
at that pace, racing,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.880
that's when you can really hurt yourself.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.320
That's probably nothing compared to that.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.212
- [Lindsey] She has a point.

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:23.460
- But also, but, great,
so both are so crazy.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.680
But like, you're going
through forests, right?

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.513
Like when you get dropped off...

00:01:26.513 --> 00:01:27.960
- No, there was, we're
above the tree line,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.930
so there was no, there
were no trees at all.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:32.310
- Like on your whole path down?

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.143
- Nope.
- Oh.

00:01:33.143 --> 00:01:34.589
- Just rocks, so avoid the rocks.

00:01:34.589 --> 00:01:35.793
(audience laughs)
Avoid the rocks.

00:01:35.793 --> 00:01:36.660
- Just rocks.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.728
- Yeah, just a couple.

00:01:37.728 --> 00:01:38.561
(Lindsey chuckles)

00:01:38.561 --> 00:01:39.394
- Those are handy.
- Yeah.

00:01:39.394 --> 00:01:41.310
- Okay, wait, you had
such a great vacation.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.150
That's awesome.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.020
Have you been heliskiing?

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:43.853
Have you ever jumped out?

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:44.746
- I have, I have.

00:01:44.746 --> 00:01:45.579
- You have?

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:46.412
- [Lindsey] Yeah, that's
why we're besties.

00:01:46.412 --> 00:01:47.580
- [Chelsea] Yeah, we're friends, we're,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.170
we actually haven't skied
together yet, though.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.820
But we will, we will ski together.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.141
- [Lindsey] Eventually, if
she's never, not on tour.

00:01:53.141 --> 00:01:53.974
- [Kelly] You've jumped
out of a helicopter?

00:01:53.974 --> 00:01:55.050
- [Chelsea] Well, we'll do it this winter.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.580
We're gonna go in Park City.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.680
- Okay, if you call me to
hang out, I will be busy.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.513
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:00.513 --> 00:02:02.190
It's like, no you won't, but if you did...

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:03.570
- You can apres ski.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.850
- You can go tubing,
while we're heliskiing.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.813
We'll drive you down
and you'll be in a tube.

00:02:07.813 --> 00:02:08.646
- [Kelly] I don't even like,

00:02:08.646 --> 00:02:09.540
like on my ranch, in Montana, you can tube

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.180
and you can ski, there's like
pretty-high slopes there.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.252
But I am terrified of even tubing.

00:02:14.252 --> 00:02:15.451
- Risk is fun.

00:02:15.451 --> 00:02:17.011
- [Kelly] It is for some.

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:18.210
(Lindsey chuckles)
It is.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.401
And some of us are so good with average.

00:02:20.401 --> 00:02:21.870
(Lindsey laughs)

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.040
So wait, so you've got a book out now.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:23.873
This is awesome.

00:02:23.873 --> 00:02:25.230
So, it's called, "Rise".

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.120
So, what, it's your story, my story.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.400
So, why did you wanna do this?

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.140
- [Lindsey] You know, I
retired from ski racing

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.360
and it was, I think
really therapeutic for me

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.830
to kind of look back at my life.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.540
And I really wanted to share some

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.120
of the lessons that I've
learned, the experiences

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.330
and I've had a lot of injuries,
a lot of personal struggles.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.340
So, you know, I again, I've learned a lot

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.560
and I, I just wanted to inspire my fans

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.000
to be their best selves.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.400
Just like, I learned
how to be in my career.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.653
- [Kelly] Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:51.653 --> 00:02:53.373
(audience applauds)

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.500
You, you recently lost your mama

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.030
and this book is dedicated to her.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.043
So how did she, how did she inspire it?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.550
- Yeah, I mean my mom has
been a huge inspiration

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.110
in my life.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:04.943
- That's awesome.

00:03:04.943 --> 00:03:06.120
- Yeah, and I, you know,

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.090
dedicated the book to her
when I found out she had ALS

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.910
and I was gonna dedicate
it to her anyways.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.440
But, she died only a few weeks ago

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:18.930
and you know, she had a stroke
when she gave birth to me.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.150
She's faced so many obstacles in her life

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.270
and it really gave me a
perspective on my life

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.490
and how I approach it and you know,

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.830
whenever I have a bad
day, I looked at my mom

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.250
and I said, "Well she has a
positive attitude, why can't I?"

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:37.250
So, she was such an inspiration
to me and it's been hard.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.170
- [Kelly] It's a really
beautiful thing though,

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.370
to know that you've had that.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.410
Like, not everybody
gets that right in life.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.940
It's such a hard thing to grieve,

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.000
but just to know, it's
such a beautiful thing too,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.710
to have had a mom that
had that kind of impact

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:50.790
that you do something cool like this

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.160
and dedicate it and know that's a reason,

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.440
one of the main reasons
why you got where you are.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.273
- Yeah.
(audience applauds)

00:03:56.273 --> 00:03:58.773
- [Kelly] It's so, really cool, beautiful.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.740
Well Lindsey, one thing that you've had

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.590
to recover from, is a ski injury in 2013.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.630
So, it led to insomnia?

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.890
- Yeah, so I mean, I've,

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.800
I had a lot of obstacles in my life,

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.370
but you know, having so many surgeries,

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.550
you know, I was laying in,
in my bed and you know,

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.130
I know as an athlete you
need sleep to recover.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.330
Everyone knows that.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.220
And, and I just struggled so much

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:26.370
after my surgeries to sleep and you know,

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.290
it's, I approached it as I
approached everything else,

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.570
you know, how do I find a solution?

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.500
And I didn't really realize

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.900
that it was actually
insomnia until much later.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.430
But I, you know, tried a lot of things

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:39.570
and I was just so thankful
that I found a solution.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.150
You know, I talked to my
doctor and Quviviq is,

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.037
you know, a new medication that I've found

00:04:44.037 --> 00:04:45.150
and I'm very thankful for.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.010
Especially now, you know, with everything

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:47.880
that's going on in my life,

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:51.030
sometimes, I just have a hard
time shutting off my mind

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.130
and you know, everyone
thinks that, you know,

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.470
not sleeping is just kind
of normal and you know,

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.730
hey, I only sleep four hours a night.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.470
That's not, not normal, we need sleep...

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.390
- That's because of society,
yeah, we don't sleep enough.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:01.770
We are always going and going and going.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:02.603
- Yeah.

00:05:02.603 --> 00:05:04.500
- To get ahead you must keep
going, like that kind of thing.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.720
- So, like one box, you
know, checked off my list

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.940
of things that I don't have
to worry about anymore.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.389
- Insomnia sucks, I used, I
used to suffer from that too.

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:12.810
And on tour it's hard,

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.510
because especially if you
get done with like a big,

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.940
race thing and, and,

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.050
and I would get done with a performance.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.120
Like, you'd get done and
your body is so amped up

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.259
that it's really hard to come down.

00:05:23.259 --> 00:05:24.092
- [Lindsey] Yeah.

00:05:24.092 --> 00:05:24.925
- Like from that adrenaline rush.

00:05:24.925 --> 00:05:25.758
- Yeah, the adrenaline rush is hard to...

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:26.742
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:05:26.742 --> 00:05:28.380
- So, I can't even imagine
at the speeds you were going

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.300
and like, you know,
near death experiences.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.410
So, that would be hard to come down from.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:32.310
I'm glad you found something.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.143
- Yeah, thank you.

00:05:33.143 --> 00:05:33.976
- [Kelly] Because man,
when you don't get sleep,

00:05:33.976 --> 00:05:35.733
I'm a, I'm not likable.

